<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>

    <style name="Theme.SlowLock" parent="android:Theme.Material.Light.NoActionBar" />

    <!--
        The theme for ShortcutLaunchActivity, which is now meant to be SEEN. This replaces
        feature 002's Theme.SlowLock.Invisible, whose entire job was the opposite.

        windowBackground is the same colour resource WaitScreen paints (research.md R7,
        obligation W12). Without that, the system paints the starting window in the app
        theme's background and the screen changes colour a frame later - a flash, on the one
        screen that must not move. With it, the tap lands on the final background immediately
        (FR-022) and the only subsequent change is the text appearing.

        A DayNight parent so the system chrome around the STARTING window follows the device's
        light/dark setting; matching only in light mode would leave a white flash at night
        (manual case M4.9). @color/wait_background itself resolves through values-night on its
        own, by configuration, whatever the parent is.

        The parent is android:Theme.DeviceDefault.DayNight rather than the
        android:Theme.Material.DayNight.NoActionBar named in tasks.md T013: the platform ships
        no Material DayNight variant at all (Theme.Material is Light or dark, never both), and
        AppCompat's DayNight would mean a new dependency this feature is forbidden to add. The
        DeviceDefault DayNight family is the only platform theme that switches, and it has no
        NoActionBar variant, so the two window attributes below do that job.

        android:windowDisablePreview is deliberately NOT carried over: the wait screen wants a
        starting window, where the invisible activity wanted none.
    -->
    <style name="Theme.SlowLock.Wait" parent="android:Theme.DeviceDefault.DayNight">
        <item name="android:windowActionBar">false</item>
        <item name="android:windowNoTitle">true</item>
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@color/wait_background</item>
    </style>
</resources>
